If a patient has a shorter-duration-opioid-use then every clinician may use a ten-percent-of-original-dose-per-week-or-slower-first-taper-stage for the patient.
If a patient has a shorter-duration-opioid-use and the patient reaches an approximately-thirty-percent-of-original-dose then every clinician may decrease a remaining-opioid-dose by an approximately-ten-percent at an interval of 1 week for the patient.
